<p>Fannie Mae issued a A$1.0 billion global bond on Wednesday through joint lead managers Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Merrill Lynch and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p>The bonds, which mature July 10, 2002, will be priced in early European time on Thursday at a spread of 19 basis points over the 9.75 percent March 2002 government bond. Payment date is July 10.</p>
<p>The World Bank also issued a A$100 million Eurobond through Hambros Bank, which matures July 15, 2002.</p>
<p>The bonds pay a 6.75 percent coupon and carry a 101.705 issue price. Payment date is July 15.</p>
